{
  "_comment": "Fill-in Funnies: Retirement Edition. One activity is one short, original retirement story with numbered blanks. The reader first writes a word for each numbered prompt (Step 1) without seeing the story, then copies the words into the matching blanks and reads the result aloud (Step 2). Placeholders are written [1], [2] ... in order of first appearance; a number may appear again later (a callback), never before its first use. Every blank's kind comes from blankKinds, whose label and hint are printed on the word list exactly as written here (frontend/src/utils/studio/fill-in-funnies/content.ts mirrors them, and a test holds the two identical). 'classes' are the grammatical slots a kind can fill; the blind checker names the slots each blank's position accepts without being told the kind, and a story survives only when every blank's kind fits. Variety is structural: every requested story gets its own brief (a situation, a format, a humour pattern and a mix of blank kinds, sampled by seed). blockedTerms keep sensitive topics, crude humour, ageist jokes and publishing risks off the page; brandTerms keep brands and celebrities off it.",
  "limits": {
    "rateLimitPerWindow": 30,
    "maxOutputTokens": 6144,
    "checkMaxOutputTokens": 3072,
    "maxAttempts": 3,
    "poolSize": 4,
    "targetStories": 1,
    "minBlanks": 8,
    "maxBlanks": 12,
    "minWords": 60,
    "maxWords": 140,
    "minParagraphs": 2,
    "maxParagraphs": 5,
    "maxParagraphWords": 60,
    "maxSentenceWords": 30,
    "maxTitleChars": 40,
    "maxTitleWords": 7,
    "maxPremiseChars": 120,
    "maxKindRepeats": 3,
    "minDistinctKinds": 6,
    "maxNameBlanks": 2,
    "maxCallbacks": 2
  },
  "locale": {
    "nativeLocales": ["en"],
    "nativeLine": "- Write in clear, warm, natural English for adults and retirees.",
    "otherLine": "- Write the title and story in language locale '{locale}', natural for that language, but keep every blank kind exactly as listed."
  },
  "mixedTheme": "everyday retirement life",
